    "name": "I \u2014 documentary-style cold open on history facts (transformation reveal)",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "nd_CPKJHNG1XTV0K5B8RPVMB56BCX",
        "kind": "prompt",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: documentary-style cold open\nTopic: history facts\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 10s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_C61C1XFDNJYMY18E25XSW76WFM",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_9SWP02JP751YX1Z32MHTCCK1FD",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_BZZYHEQZARD8TAK5SWNCZCM95N",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.77,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a documentary-style cold open about history facts for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the documentary-style cold open \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a slow push with a simultaneous barely-perceptible dutch roll on a 50mm anamorphic with 2x squeeze, framing with deep negative space above the subject with a low horizon.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with underlighting from a translucent base panel; grade as a pastel low-contrast grade with a lifted black point. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Your entire reply is the prompt itself: one dense paragraph, no title, no quotation marks, no trailing notes."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_7N8S9ZMYEPXRD105KQVN5DKHSY",
        "kind": "image-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 700
